==English==

===Etymology===
From {{affix|en|disappoint|-ment}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌdɪsəˈpɔɪntmənt/|a=UK}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˌdɪsəˈpɔɪntmənt/|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-disappointment.ogg|a=GenAm}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The feeling or state of being [[disappoint]]ed: a feeling of [[sadness]] or [[frustration]] when something is not as good as one [[hope]]d or [[expect]]ed, or when something bad unexpectedly happens.
#: {{ux|en|Even a trip to beautiful California can cause '''disappointment'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Landon Francesca Carrara|page=184|volume=II|text=They remembered too keenly their pleasant credulity as to what to-morrow would bring forth, to dare indulge expectation of its pleasure; they had been disappointed once—so might they be again—for '''disappointment''' ever leaves fear behind.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1992|title=Today|author=News Group Newspapers Ltd
|passage=Choking back his disappointment after his own team's splendid wins against Liverpool and Aston Villa, he said: "I've got to be humble and say we were beaten by a very good side."}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} An example or the act of disappointing: a circumstance in which a positive [[expectation]] is not achieved.
#: {{ux|en|The '''disappointment''' with our trip to California caused bickering.}}
#* {{quote-journal
|en
|date=May 5, 2012
|author=Phil McNulty
|title=Chelsea 2-1 Liverpool
|work=BBC Sport
|url=http://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/0/football/17878435
|page=
|passage=For Liverpool, their season will now be regarded as a relative '''disappointment''' after failure to add the FA Cup to the Carling Cup and not mounting a challenge to reach the Champions League places.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1990|author=Peter Hennessy|title=Cabinet|publisher=Basil Blackwell Ltd
|passage=As the '''disappointments''' crowded in &mdash; the economy, Rhodesia, strife within the trade-union movement &mdash; [[w:Harold Wilson|Wilson]] tried the expedient of a semi-formal inner Cabinet, or Parliamentary Committee, as he misleadingly liked to call it.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} Something or someone that disappoints: that which [[cause]]s disappointment.
#: {{ux|en|Even a trip to beautiful California can be a '''disappointment'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|What a '''disappointment'''!}}

====Usage notes====
Used with the prepositions ''at/with/over''.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|let-down}}
* {{l|en|setback}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|disappoint}}

